Z||000000||bHooper||02-29-2000||02:58 PM||||I have a question; what is to much to pay for a parts car?<BR>    I am in discusion's with a local salvage yard, about purchasing a '86 4 banger 5 speed.  They have had the car for 6-7 years and have only sold a headlight motor off of it.  The paint is rough, it has a sunroof (w/good glass) and the carpet appears decent.  The keys have been locked up in the trunk, but they <B>swear</B> it ran before... "just needed some carb work"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>    I need the tranny to fix my GT, and the carpet wouldn't be bad, either.  If I can get the car for anything less than the $400 they are asking, is it a fair deal?  Do you think I could make enough from selling the things I dont need; ie: sunroof, ect... to compensate for the price?  <P>thanks,<BR>Brian Hooper||||reg||5
